{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791651535,"nonce":"4ukTBc3SG39I4SvuD/U+B28/kZY=","message":"Slice 2 (new classes, so child components) is on branch hot-reload-classes: 091399b9, 138d348e, ac054e88, ab68c726, 98cbb041. Not on main yet.\n\nA reload now takes a program that adds a class with its methods and statics, and the string literals and function types (handler types) that come with one. The new program's types, globals and functions are numbered onto the running ones. The tables have spare room, so compiled code reads them in place. What a new class needs from the new entry function (its descriptor and the first values of its statics) is cut out of that function and run once after the reload.\n\nA class the new program drops stays in the tables, so one a later reload adds back is the class that was running, statics included.\n\nashui's tests/fixtures/hotreload v5 prints \"reloaded v5 count=5 width=50.000000000 height=20.000000000 probe=zz/2\" with the default tiers, --jit-threshold 1, cranelift and llvm.\n\nStill refused: a method or static added to a class that was already running (this includes the first use of a standard library static such as Type.getClassName or Math.floor, which adds fields to the $Class object), enum constructor changes, and a class setup that depends on control flow. Methods added to an existing class are the next slice.","files":null}]}